==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|what}} + {{term|soever}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌwɒtsəʊˈɛvə/}}, {{SAMPA|/%wQt.s@U"ev.@r/}}
* {{audio|en-us-whatsoever.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɛvə(r)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[whatever|Whatever]].
#: ''“In '''whatsoever''' shape he lurk”.'' (Milton)
#: ''“'''Whatsoever''' God hath said unto thee, do”.'' (Gen. xxxi. 16)
# In any way; [[at all]].
#: ''He gave me no answer '''whatsoever'''.''

